title: 'Decide: should a refresh restart the idle countdown in full, keeping a chatty
  list_changed child alive?'
updated: 2026-11-10T12:11:56Z
---

From k129. Since k129 a refresh of a running upstream counts as in flight (Upstream::_held_p) and, like a call, starts the full idle countdown again when it ends. A child that sends notifications/tools/list_changed more often than idle_timeout -- each answered with a refresh -- is then never stopped when idle, against the hub's RAM goal. Options: (A, current, worker's choice) a refresh counts like a call: full countdown from its end. (B) a refresh holds the countdown off while it runs but does not touch last_used: at its end the countdown resumes from the end of the last call, stopping at once if that is already past. Maintainer call.

Decision by the main session (2026-11-10), under the maintainer's 'erledige die tickets von karr'; the maintainer may veto: (B). A refresh holds the idle countdown off while it runs but does not touch last_used, so a chatty list_changed child is still stopped when idle (the RAM goal).

